INT. DRYDOCK CANTEEN - NIGHT

Steel table. Cold tea. A hull looms through the window, half-painted.

ODALYS VANTERPOOL (50s, foreman, grease-stained clipboard) stands. Doesn't sit.

BRANIMIR KOSTA (60s, welder, one good eye) stares at his hands.

KIRIN ASHWORTH (19, apprentice, new boots) hovers by the door.

BIG HOLLIS (40s, union steward, arms folded) leans on the vending machine.

ODALYS
(to the room)
Listen up. Inspection failed. Weld seam forty-two.

Silence.

BRANIMIR
(muttering)
Forty-two. Forty-two.

ODALYS
Branimir.

BRANIMIR
I heard.

ODALYS
Who signed off on it?

HOLLIS
Does it matter?

ODALYS
It matters.

KIRIN
It was me.

Everyone turns.

KIRIN (CONT'D)
Branimir was on break. I did the pass. I thought it was good.

BRANIMIR
It wasn't him.

KIRIN
It was.

BRANIMIR
Boy, sit down.

ODALYS
Kirin, did you X-ray the seam?

KIRIN
No ma'am. There was no film left.

HOLLIS
No film. On a Tuesday.

ODALYS
Who's in charge of ordering film?

HOLLIS
You are.

ODALYS
Right.
(beat)
Right.

BRANIMIR
So it's your film. Your seam. Your hull.

ODALYS
Don't.

BRANIMIR
Forty years I never missed a seam.

ODALYS
I know.

BRANIMIR
Forty years.

ODALYS
I know, Branimir.

HOLLIS
Nobody gets fired tonight.

ODALYS
Not your call.

HOLLIS
It's the contract.

ODALYS
The contract says a lot of things.

BRANIMIR
The ship sails Friday.

ODALYS
The ship does not sail Friday.

KIRIN
Is it really that bad?

ODALYS
It's a hairline crack, Kirin. At sea it opens like a zipper.

Her hand slams the table. Tea jumps. Kirin flinches.

Branimir laughs. Short. Dry.

BRANIMIR
Then we cut it out. Tonight. Four of us.

ODALYS
(quietly)
Four of us.

HOLLIS
Overtime's on the union.

ODALYS
(to herself)
Film. I forgot the film.

She picks up the clipboard. Puts it down. Picks up four mugs instead.

ODALYS (CONT'D)
Tea's cold. I'll make fresh.
